  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU contribution to the Pandemic Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The   Pandemic   Fund   is   a   major   international   instrument   in   the   current   global   health  architecture  for  pandemic  prevention,  preparedness  and  response.  The  EU  contribution  will  enhance  health  security  globally  by  strengthening  the  weakest  identified  links  in  the  highest  risk geographical areas. The Pandemic Fund will allocate funding where investments are most  urgently needed and focus on bridging key capacity gaps, including but not limited to support  country  capacity  to  assist  public  health  workforce  in  low&#xbf; and  middle-income  countries; community  and  primary  health  care;  regional  and  global  health  institutions;  regulatory harmonisation; capacity to address spill-over risks from the animal health domain; laboratory systems; better disease surveillance, reporting and information sharing; logistical capacity for countermeasures and medical supplies; financial support to technical assistance and analytics.</narrative>
  </description>
